1
00:00:06,200 --> 00:00:06,600
Daniel

2
00:00:07,066 --> 00:00:07,900
Don't you think

3
00:00:07,900 --> 00:00:09,433
my skills are worthless

4
00:00:09,633 --> 00:00:10,833
Then I'll use those skills

5
00:00:11,200 --> 00:00:12,367
to raise these forest frogs

6
00:00:12,633 --> 00:00:13,800
And I'll pay you back

7
00:00:13,800 --> 00:00:15,200
for every insult you gave me

8
00:00:17,533 --> 00:00:18,333
James, it's Lewes

9
00:00:18,366 --> 00:00:19,400
Do you have any cash

10
00:00:19,500 --> 00:00:20,166
Lend me twenty thousand

11
00:00:20,166 --> 00:00:20,966
- Uncle
- Yes, emergency

12
00:00:21,100 --> 00:00:22,233
Can you lend me twenty thousand

13
00:00:23,733 --> 00:00:25,027
I've spent all my savings

14
00:00:25,400 --> 00:00:26,900
and borrowed from everyone I could

15
00:00:27,100 --> 00:00:28,333
I must succeed this time

16
00:00:28,333 --> 00:00:29,300
I can't afford to fail

17
00:00:32,233 --> 00:00:34,200
To ensure high-quality oil

18
00:00:34,200 --> 00:00:35,967
you need enough water

19
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:36,967
and good water quality

20
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:39,500
Plus my special feed

21
00:00:39,733 --> 00:00:40,770
mealworms

22
00:00:46,366 --> 00:00:46,833
Lewes

23
00:00:47,200 --> 00:00:48,800
I heard you're not working for Daniel

24
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:50,567
and rented a place to raise frogs yourself

25
00:00:50,600 --> 00:00:51,600
Isn't that ridiculous

26
00:00:51,600 --> 00:00:52,533
Do you even know how

27
00:00:52,766 --> 00:00:54,433
Don't lose your parents' life savings

28
00:00:54,733 --> 00:00:55,333
Lewes

29
00:00:55,433 --> 00:00:57,000
Raising forest frogs isn't easy

30
00:00:57,200 --> 00:00:57,900
One mistake

31
00:00:57,900 --> 00:00:59,000
and you'll lose everything

32
00:00:59,200 --> 00:01:00,233
Better to stay with your brother-in-law

33
00:01:00,433 --> 00:01:01,367
It's a steady paycheck

34
00:01:02,100 --> 00:01:03,366
I heard Daniel

35
00:01:03,400 --> 00:01:04,733
made three million this time

36
00:01:04,733 --> 00:01:06,000
How much is he paying you

37
00:01:11,766 --> 00:01:12,433
Brother-in-law

38
00:01:12,866 --> 00:01:14,066
I heard you rented

39
00:01:14,066 --> 00:01:15,133
the greenhouse across the way

40
00:01:15,433 --> 00:01:16,300
Are you crazy

41
00:01:16,700 --> 00:01:17,900
I gave you fifty thousand

42
00:01:17,900 --> 00:01:19,833
was for you and Cynthia to live a good life

43
00:01:19,933 --> 00:01:21,400
not to throw it down the drain

44
00:01:21,466 --> 00:01:22,500
Fifty thousand

45
00:01:22,600 --> 00:01:23,300
The Liu family

46
00:01:23,300 --> 00:01:24,867
has a real spendthrift now

47
00:01:25,333 --> 00:01:26,800
Daniel made a fortune

48
00:01:26,833 --> 00:01:27,800
and cared for his sister

49
00:01:27,800 --> 00:01:29,633
but this loser is wasting it all

50
00:01:29,833 --> 00:01:31,233
For Cynthia to be with him

51
00:01:31,566 --> 00:01:33,367
is the worst luck ever

52
00:01:33,367 --> 00:01:34,433
If I lose, I'll take it

53
00:01:34,433 --> 00:01:35,600
Lewes, are you stupid

54
00:01:35,766 --> 00:01:37,000
50,000, not 500

55
00:01:37,200 --> 00:01:38,100
You're a grown man

56
00:01:38,100 --> 00:01:39,600
How are you less mature than Daniel

57
00:01:39,600 --> 00:01:41,000
No wonder he's getting rich

58
00:01:41,033 --> 00:01:41,933
It's just small change

59
00:01:41,933 --> 00:01:43,500
I'm hatching five times the tadpoles this time

60
00:01:43,533 --> 00:01:44,200
Once they mature

61
00:01:44,233 --> 00:01:45,267
I'll have millions coming in

62
00:01:45,433 --> 00:01:46,200
Lewes

63
00:01:46,366 --> 00:01:48,033
When you're too broke to eat

64
00:01:48,233 --> 00:01:49,333
you can still come work for me

65
00:01:50,066 --> 00:01:51,233
Daniel is so generous

66
00:01:51,433 --> 00:01:52,433
Unlike some people

67
00:01:52,766 --> 00:01:54,300
who get jealous of others' success

68
00:01:56,900 --> 00:01:58,833
I'll raise the best frogs ever

69
00:01:59,233 --> 00:02:00,133
When that time comes

70
00:02:00,733 --> 00:02:02,533
no one will dare look down on me

71
00:02:09,200 --> 00:02:10,300
The quality of the oil

72
00:02:10,600 --> 00:02:11,500
is everything

73
00:02:11,733 --> 00:02:13,033
One degree difference in temperature

74
00:02:13,033 --> 00:02:14,567
and the oil quality drops a level

75
00:02:14,567 --> 00:02:15,767
One missing ingredient in the feed

76
00:02:15,767 --> 00:02:17,100
and the yield drops by ten percent

77
00:02:17,333 --> 00:02:18,266
Daniel

78
00:02:18,266 --> 00:02:20,933
You think it's just throwing them into the water

79
00:02:21,266 --> 00:02:22,366
Without my expertise

80
00:02:22,567 --> 00:02:23,533
those frogs of yours

81
00:02:23,533 --> 00:02:24,933
won't sell for a penny
